    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nSometimes, I want to change a comment, but not actually get rid of it. Other times, I want to completely remove the comment altogether. `mini.comment` only currently provides one textobject, but I wish it would provide multiple - which could be easily scoped to `ic` and `ac`. If we don't want to mess with `c`, since it may confuse people expecting `change`, it could bind to something else by default - I just think the functionality would be useful.",
