            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I didn't quite proof read the whole code snippet, but just one stylistic thing that I'd change is the computation of `get_start_col` and `offset`:\n\n```lua\n  local get_start_col = ai_type == \"a\" and vim.fn.match or vim.fn.matchend\n  local offset = ai_type == \"a\" and 0 or 1\n```\n\nBut as I already said [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1431#issuecomment-3007543898), using `vim.fn.match()` without validation is not really the best approach here.",
