        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "That's a lot cleaner, thanks!\n\nI worked a bit on making the code you sent use `vim.bo.comments` instead of `vim.bo.commentstring`, so I could handle languages with multiple commentstrings. I was able to get it working for languages like Rust, but it seems to [grow in complexity for other languages](https://neovim.io/doc/user/change.html#format-comments).\n\nDo you think I should instead try relying on Treesitter to get the commentstring like `mini.comment`? Obviously it still won't support doc comments, but that's a regex fight I don't expect to win today.",
            "created_at": "2025-06-26T21:55:59Z",
