            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Do you think I should instead try relying on Treesitter to get the commentstring like `mini.comment`?\n\n'mini.comment' uses tree-sitter to account for cases when in there several *languages* within same buffer. Like in markdown code blocks, for example. This allows to get proper commentstring based on cursor position.\n\n> I worked a bit on making the code you sent use `vim.bo.comments` instead of `vim.bo.commentstring`, so I could handle languages with multiple commentstrings. I was able to get it working for languages like Rust, but it seems to [grow in complexity for other languages](https://neovim.io/doc/user/change.html#format-comments).\n\nYou can take a look at how ['mini.snippets' uses 'comments' to detect if cursor is inside comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/145476d74aaa3236db9dc6705d0fa3eb0f4f8352/lua/mini/snippets.lua#L2584). But for comment toggling I'd suggest sticking with 'commentstring', as *adding* comment still needs only a single comment leader.",
            "created_at": "2025-06-27T07:57:11Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1837#issuecomment-3012091643",
