        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Using the vanilla `mini.comment` functionality, I can use the textobject to select the entire `///` doc comments, as well as normal `//` comments. That's not stored in the Rust `vim.bo.commentstring`, so it has to be tree-sitter giving us that, right?\n\nWith 'mini.comment' it is only possible in this example to do something like `dgc` / `cgc` / `ygc` to delete/change/yank the entire comment textobject. It is because `/// xxx` matches the comment structure defined by `// %s` value of 'commentstring' ('mini.comment' ignores whitespace between `//` and `%s`, so `/// xxx` is just a commented `/ xxx` string).\n\nToggling comment of the line `/// xxx` makes it `/ xxx`. If it does anything else for you, then it is either 1) a smart setting of 'commentstring' (maybe); 2) some other tree-sitter parser injected specifically for docstrings (unlikely); 3) there is some misunderstanding (likely).",
